WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.640
Today we are talking about Sleeping Beauty in&nbsp;
the form of the Sleeping Beauty Paradox. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:10.500
goes as follows: Sleeping Beauty is going&nbsp;
to be put to sleep on a Sunday - I should&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:16.080
clarify Sleeping Beauty has agreed to do this&nbsp;
and knows all of the details of the experiment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:22.080
this is important. Sleeping Beauty is put to sleep&nbsp;
on Sunday. A coin is then flipped; if the coin is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:27.540
tails we are going to wake her up on Monday, we&nbsp;
then ask her some questions, and then she's put&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:34.380
back to sleep with some amnesia inducing drug so&nbsp;
she has no memory that she was ever awake. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:39.240
is again very important to the setup. And then&nbsp;
we also - same thing - wake her up on Tuesday,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:44.400
ask the same questions, put back to sleep. And&nbsp;
again she has no idea. If the coin was heads,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:50.100
she's woken up on Monday only, asked questions,&nbsp;
perhaps with the same amnesia inducing drugs.&nbsp;

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:58.080
Sleeping Beauty is put to sleep, we flip&nbsp;
a coin. If it's tails we wake her up on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:02.400
Monday, ask her some questions, put her back&nbsp;
to sleep. She doesn't know it was Monday, she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:06.060
doesn't know what happened to the coin, she&nbsp;
has no idea when she wakes up what's going on.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:10.980
Put back to sleep with no memory of&nbsp;
that incident. She's woken up on Tuesday,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:16.680
same thing, ask questions, put back to sleep;&nbsp;
has no idea it's Tuesday or what's happened.&nbsp;

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:21.540
Or if it was heads we just wake her up the once&nbsp;
and then ask her the questions, put her back to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:26.880
sleep, nothing happens on the Tuesday; and in both&nbsp;
cases the experiment ends on Wednesday. So she's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:33.420
woken up and she's free. And she knows all of this&nbsp;
before the experiment begins, so she is aware that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:39.300
she may be woken up twice or once depending on&nbsp;
the outcome of the flip of that coin. 
