00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:55.500
two situations. Now we have law of conditional&nbsp;
probability tells us the probability of A given&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.500 --> 00:06:01.380
B is the probability of A intersect B divided by&nbsp;
the probability of B. So we can apply this here and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:08.100
say, so this one is the probability of Monday and&nbsp;
tails divided by the probability of being tails;&nbsp;

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:14.340
and this one is the probability of Tuesday and&nbsp;
tails divided by the probability of being tails.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:19.140
These two are equal so it doesn't matter what's on&nbsp;
the bottom, multiply through. Having assumed it was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:24.780
tails, our conclusion we can draw is that these two&nbsp;
things are equal because they're all on the same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:32.040
side of the equation. So we can say the probability&nbsp;
of Monday and tails is equal to the probability&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:41.220
of Tuesday and tails. Okay, now that was assuming&nbsp;
