00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:37.440
are equal, they both have the same denominator&nbsp;
so we ignore it, so therefore the probability of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:44.820
tails and Monday equals the probability of heads&nbsp;
and Monday. Now we have this equation and we have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:49.500
this equation. So we've got Monday and tails; tails&nbsp;
and Monday, they're the same thing. In both cases&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:54.480
it's a Monday and tails is flipped. So this one's&nbsp;
equal to Tuesday and tails and same thing is also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:59.400
equal to heads on Monday. So what we've done here&nbsp;
is actually shown that these are like equal, all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:06.180
three things are the same, and all three of them&nbsp;
are exactly case 1, case 2, and case 3 of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.180 --> 00:08:11.340
our original list. We made some assumptions, did&nbsp;
some conditional probability, and it allowed us&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:18.780
to arrive at the conclusion that all three of&nbsp;
our situations actually are equally likely to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.780 --> 00:08:26.640
occur. The total probability has to be 1.
These are the three possible events, they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:32.220
are all equally likely, their total probability&nbsp;
has to be 1 - it's the law of total probability.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:37.980
The only solution then is that each individual&nbsp;
